<h2 id="part-h">Part H: Formal Terms &amp; Execution</h2>
<h3 id="s35">35. General Contract Terms</h3>
<p>The following general terms apply to the interpretation and administration of this Agreement.</p>
<h4 id="s35-1">35.1 Entire Agreement</h4>
<p>This Agreement, including its Schedules and any written terms expressly incorporated into it, constitutes the agreement between Apex Feeds and the Retailer concerning the Retailer’s participation in the Apex Feeds wholesale program.</p>
<p>It replaces previous discussions, representations or understandings concerning the same subject matter to the extent they are inconsistent with this Agreement. This clause does not exclude liability for fraudulent, misleading or deceptive conduct or any other matter that cannot lawfully be excluded.</p>
<h4 id="s35-2">35.2 Agreement Documents</h4>
<p>This Agreement includes:</p>
<ul>
<li>the main body of the Authorised Retailer Agreement &amp; Brand Standards;</li>
<li>Schedule A — Product Storage &amp; Handling Standards;</li>
<li>Schedule B — Approved Advertising &amp; Brand Standards;</li>
<li>Schedule C — Returns &amp; Claims Procedure;</li>
<li>Schedule D — Retailer Claim Form; and</li>
<li>any other document expressly stated in writing to form part of this Agreement.</li>
</ul>
<p>General marketing materials, social media posts, informal conversations or ordinary product information do not amend this Agreement merely because they relate to Apex Feeds products.</p>
<h4 id="s35-3">35.3 Order of Precedence</h4>
<p>Where there is an inconsistency between documents forming part of this Agreement, the following order applies unless expressly stated otherwise:</p>
<p>1. any written variation specifically agreed between Apex Feeds and the Retailer;</p>
<p>2. the main body of this Agreement;</p>
<p>3. the applicable Schedule; and 4. other written standards expressly incorporated into the Agreement.</p>
<p>However, a specific product-safety, recall, storage or legal instruction issued for a particular product or Batch takes priority to the extent reasonably necessary to address that specific issue.</p>
<h4 id="s35-4">35.4 Changes to the Agreement</h4>
<p>This Agreement may be updated in accordance with Section 29. A material contractual change will not take effect merely because an Apex Feeds employee makes an informal statement inconsistent with the Agreement. Where the parties specifically agree to vary a material contractual term for a particular Retailer, that variation should be recorded in writing.</p>
<h4 id="s35-5">35.5 No Waiver</h4>
<p>If either party does not immediately enforce a right under this Agreement, that does not automatically mean the party has permanently waived that right.</p>
<p>A waiver of a particular breach or requirement does not automatically waive:</p>
<ul>
<li>a later breach;</li>
<li>a different breach; or</li>
<li>future compliance with the applicable requirement.</li>
</ul>
<p>Where previous conduct has reasonably created uncertainty about a requirement, the affected party should clarify its position before treating continued conduct as deliberate non-compliance where reasonably appropriate.</p>
<h4 id="s35-6">35.6 Severability</h4>
<p>If a provision of this Agreement is found to be invalid, unlawful or unenforceable, that provision is to be read down to the extent reasonably possible so that it operates lawfully. If it cannot reasonably be read down, the affected provision or part may be severed without invalidating the remainder of the Agreement, to the extent permitted by law.</p>
<h4 id="s35-7">35.7 No Partnership, Agency or Franchise</h4>
<p>Nothing in this Agreement creates a partnership, joint venture, employment relationship, franchise or agency between Apex Feeds and the Retailer. The Retailer operates its own independent business and purchases Apex Feeds products for resale in accordance with this Agreement.</p>
<p>Neither party may bind the other or enter into commitments on the other’s behalf unless separately authorised in writing.</p>
<h4 id="s35-8">35.8 Independent Business Decisions</h4>
<p>Except for obligations expressly established by this Agreement or applicable law, each party remains responsible for its own independent business decisions.</p>
<p>The Retailer independently determines matters including its:</p>
<ul>
<li>retail pricing;</li>
<li>staffing;</li>
<li>business hours;</li>
<li>store layout;</li>
<li>customer relationships;</li>
<li>ordinary marketing decisions;</li>
<li>business expenses; and</li>
<li>other operational matters.</li>
</ul>
<p>Nothing in this Agreement gives Apex Feeds general management or control over the Retailer’s independent business.</p>
<h4 id="s35-9">35.9 Assignment by the Retailer</h4>
<p>The Retailer must not assign or transfer its rights under this Agreement to another legal entity, ABN, purchaser, franchisee, licensee or unrelated third party without Apex Feeds’ prior written approval. This does not prevent ordinary internal administration within the same approved legal entity. Changes in ownership or legal entity are dealt with under Section 2.</p>
<h4 id="s35-10">35.10 Assignment by Apex Feeds</h4>
<p>Apex Feeds may assign or transfer this Agreement as part of a genuine sale, restructure or transfer of all or a substantial part of the Apex Feeds business or wholesale operations, provided that doing so does not materially reduce the Retailer’s existing rights under this Agreement. Where reasonably practicable, affected Retailers will be notified of a material transfer.</p>
<h4 id="s35-11">35.11 Subcontractors and Service Providers</h4>
<p>Either party may use employees, contractors, freight providers, professional advisers, technology providers or other service providers to perform ordinary functions associated with its business. Using a third-party service provider does not remove a party’s responsibility for obligations that remain its responsibility under this Agreement.</p>
<h4 id="s35-12">35.12 Notices</h4>
<p>Where this Agreement requires written notice, notice may be provided by:</p>
<ul>
<li>email to the latest nominated business email address;</li>
<li>the Apex Feeds wholesale account or portal where the system provides an appropriate written notification;</li>
<li>letter to the latest nominated business address; or</li>
<li>another written communication method agreed between the parties.</li>
</ul>
<p>The parties are responsible for keeping their nominated contact details reasonably current.</p>
<h4 id="s35-13">35.13 Receipt of Electronic Notices</h4>
<p>An electronic notice will ordinarily be treated as received when it is successfully sent to the latest nominated address or account and is not returned or identified as undeliverable. This does not prevent a party from showing that, because of a genuine technical or delivery failure, the notice was not reasonably capable of being received. Urgent safety or recall communications may be sent through multiple available contact methods.</p>
<h4 id="s35-14">35.14 Business Days</h4>
<p>Unless otherwise stated, a Business Day means a day other than a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday in New South Wales. Where a period expressed in Business Days ends on a non-Business Day, the relevant period continues to the next Business Day unless the context requires otherwise.</p>
<p>Specific operational cut-off times, dispatch days and safety-reporting periods stated elsewhere in this Agreement continue to apply according to their own wording.</p>
<h4 id="s35-15">35.15 References to Days</h4>
<p>Unless expressly stated as Business Days, references to days mean calendar days. A reference to a number of hours means elapsed hours and is not limited to business hours. This is particularly relevant to requirements such as the 24-hour live-arrival claim period under Section 17.</p>
<h4 id="s35-16">35.16 Headings</h4>
<p>Section headings and subheadings are included to make this Agreement easier to navigate. They do not independently create obligations or limit the meaning of the substantive provisions beneath them.</p>
<h4 id="s35-17">35.17 Singular and Plural</h4>
<p>Unless the context requires otherwise:</p>
<ul>
<li>a reference to the singular includes the plural and vice versa;</li>
<li>a reference to a person includes an individual, company or other legal entity where appropriate;</li>
<li>“including” does not limit the words preceding it; and</li>
<li>examples are illustrative and do not necessarily limit the broader provision in which they appear.</li>
</ul>
<h4 id="s35-18">35.18 References to Apex Feeds</h4>
<p>In this Agreement, “Apex Feeds” means APEX FEEDS AUST PTY LTD (ABN 37 678 568 501) unless the context clearly refers specifically to an Apex Feeds product, brand or trading identity.</p>
<h4 id="s35-19">35.19 References to the Retailer</h4>
<p>“Retailer” means the legal entity approved by Apex Feeds for wholesale supply and identified in the execution or account details associated with this Agreement. Where that entity operates multiple approved locations under the same legal entity and ABN, references to the Retailer include those locations where relevant.</p>
<h4 id="s35-20">35.20 References to Writing</h4>
<p>A requirement that something be provided “in writing” may ordinarily be satisfied by an appropriate email, electronic document, wholesale account communication or other reproducible written electronic communication. A telephone conversation or verbal discussion alone does not constitute a written variation of this Agreement.</p>
<h4 id="s35-21">35.21 Electronic Execution</h4>
<p>This Agreement may be signed electronically. Electronic signatures, electronic acceptance or counterparts may be used to the extent permitted by applicable law and any process adopted by Apex Feeds for execution of the Agreement.</p>
<p>The parties do not need to sign the same physical copy for their signatures to form part of the same Agreement.</p>
<h4 id="s35-22">35.22 Counterparts</h4>
<p>This Agreement may be executed in counterparts. Each signed counterpart forms part of the same Agreement and together they constitute one instrument.</p>
<h4 id="s35-23">35.23 Governing Law</h4>
<p>This Agreement is governed by the laws of New South Wales, Australia. Subject to any right or procedure that cannot lawfully be excluded, the parties submit to the jurisdiction of the courts and tribunals of New South Wales and courts competent to hear appeals from them.</p>
<h4 id="s35-24">35.24 Good-Faith</h4>
<p>Resolution of Disputes Where a dispute arises concerning this Agreement, the parties should first attempt to resolve the matter through direct communication between appropriately authorised representatives. Either party may provide relevant information, explain its position and propose a reasonable resolution. Nothing in this clause prevents either party from obtaining legal advice at any time.</p>
<h4 id="s35-25">35.25 Urgent Action</h4>
<p>The requirement to attempt direct resolution does not prevent either party from taking urgent action where reasonably necessary to: * protect animal or product safety; * comply with a recall or regulatory requirement; * protect confidential information or intellectual property; * preserve a legal right; * prevent significant continuing loss; or * seek urgent court or regulatory relief.</p>
<h4 id="s35-26">35.26 Costs of Own Advice</h4>
<p>Unless otherwise agreed or ordered by a court or tribunal, each party is responsible for the cost of obtaining its own legal, accounting or professional advice concerning this Agreement. Nothing in this clause alters the debt-recovery provisions applying to properly overdue amounts under Section 4.</p>
<h4 id="s35-27">35.27 Further Cooperation</h4>
<p>Each party must take reasonable steps and provide reasonable information necessary to give practical effect to obligations already established under this Agreement. This clause does not create a general obligation to perform additional services, incur substantial new costs or surrender legal rights not otherwise required by the Agreement.</p>
<h4 id="s35-28">35.28 No Third-Party Rights</h4>
<p>Except where applicable law provides otherwise, this Agreement is between Apex Feeds and the approved Retailer and does not create contractual rights for unrelated third parties merely because they may benefit from the parties’ performance of the Agreement. This does not affect customer rights arising independently under consumer law or another applicable law.</p>
<h4 id="s35-29">35.29 Continuing Effect</h4>
<p>Any provision which expressly or by its nature is intended to continue after termination will survive termination to the extent necessary to give that provision effect. This includes the continuing matters identified in Section 34.</p>
<h4 id="s35-30">35.30 Applicable Law Prevails</h4>
<p>If a provision of this Agreement conflicts with a mandatory requirement of applicable law, the mandatory legal requirement prevails to the extent of the inconsistency. Nothing in this Agreement is intended to exclude, restrict or modify a right, guarantee, remedy, obligation or liability where doing so would be unlawful.</p>
<h3 id="s36">36. Acknowledgement</h3>
<p>By signing or otherwise formally accepting this Agreement, the Retailer confirms that it wishes to participate in the Apex Feeds wholesale program as an Authorised Retailer and agrees to comply with the terms and standards applicable to that relationship.</p>
<h4 id="s36-1">36.1 Authority to Enter the Agreement</h4>
<p>The person accepting this Agreement on behalf of the Retailer confirms that they are authorised to enter into this Agreement on behalf of the legal entity identified as the Retailer. Where the Retailer is a company, the person accepting the Agreement confirms that they have appropriate authority to act for that company.</p>
<h4 id="s36-2">36.2 Accuracy of Retailer Information</h4>
<p>The Retailer confirms that information materially relevant to its wholesale application and Authorised Retailer status is, to the best of its knowledge, accurate and not materially misleading.</p>
<p>This includes applicable information concerning:</p>
<ul>
<li>legal business name;</li>
<li>ABN;</li>
<li>trading name;</li>
<li>physical retail location or locations;</li>
<li>contact information;</li>
<li>authorised representatives;</li>
<li>billing information; and</li>
<li>other information reasonably required to establish or administer the wholesale account.</li>
</ul>
<p>An innocent administrative error does not automatically constitute a breach where it is corrected within a reasonable period after discovery.</p>
<h4 id="s36-3">36.3 Opportunity to Review</h4>
<p>The Retailer acknowledges that it has been provided with, or given reasonable access to, this Agreement and its applicable Schedules before acceptance. The Retailer has had the opportunity to review the Agreement and seek independent legal, accounting or other professional advice if it considers such advice necessary. Nothing in this clause represents that the Retailer was required to obtain independent advice before entering the Agreement.</p>
<h4 id="s36-4">36.4 Understanding of the Wholesale Relationship</h4>
<p>The Retailer acknowledges that Authorised Retailer status establishes an independent wholesale supplier and retailer relationship. It does not create a partnership, franchise, employment relationship, joint venture or agency between Apex Feeds and the Retailer.</p>
<h4 id="s36-5">36.5 Compliance With Applicable Standards</h4>
<p>The Retailer agrees to take reasonable steps to ensure that Apex Feeds products under its control are purchased, stored, handled, advertised, represented and sold in accordance with the applicable requirements of this Agreement. The Retailer also acknowledges its responsibility for ensuring that relevant employees and representatives have access to information reasonably necessary for their roles.</p>
<h4 id="s36-6">36.6 Product Storage and Handling</h4>
<p>The Retailer acknowledges that different Apex Feeds product categories may require different storage and handling conditions.</p>
<p>This may include specific requirements for:</p>
<ul>
<li>shelf-stable products;</li>
<li>frozen products;</li>
<li>live feeder insects;</li>
<li>opened or prepared products; and</li>
<li>products subject to a Batch hold, withdrawal or recall.</li>
</ul>
<p>The applicable requirements are contained within this Agreement, Schedule A and relevant Apex Feeds product information.</p>
<h4 id="s36-7">36.7 Product Information and Representation</h4>
<p>The Retailer acknowledges that Apex Feeds provides product information to assist Retailers in accurately explaining and promoting its products. Retailers may use their own knowledge and communicate in their own words as permitted by this Agreement but must not knowingly attribute materially false, misleading or unsupported claims to Apex Feeds or its products.</p>
<h4 id="s36-8">36.8 Independent Retail Pricing</h4>
<p>The Retailer acknowledges that any Recommended Retail Price provided by Apex Feeds is a recommendation only. The Retailer independently determines its own retail and advertised prices, subject to applicable law. Nothing in this Agreement requires the Retailer to sell or advertise Apex Feeds products at or above a particular minimum price.</p>
<h4 id="s36-9">36.9 Authorised Sales Channels</h4>
<p>The Retailer acknowledges that Authorised Retailer status permits sale through the channels approved under Section 8 and does not automatically authorise wholesale redistribution, third-party marketplace sales or supply to unrelated businesses for onward commercial resale.</p>
<h4 id="s36-10">36.10 Product Traceability and Safety</h4>
<p>The Retailer acknowledges the importance of preserving applicable Batch Numbers and Best Before Dates and cooperating reasonably with legitimate product-quality, safety, withdrawal and recall processes. Nothing in this acknowledgement requires the Retailer to maintain customer-level Batch records for ordinary retail transactions beyond the requirements otherwise established by this Agreement or applicable law.</p>
<h4 id="s36-11">36.11 Changes During the Relationship</h4>
<p>The Retailer acknowledges that Apex Feeds products, packaging, product information and reasonable wholesale standards may develop or change over time in accordance with Section 29. Material changes to contractual obligations will be communicated in accordance with the notice provisions established by this Agreement.</p>
<h4 id="s36-12">36.12 No Guarantee of Supply or Commercial Performance</h4>
<p>The Retailer acknowledges that approval as an Authorised Retailer does not guarantee:</p>
<ul>
<li>availability of every Apex Feeds product at all times;</li>
<li>any particular level of sales or customer demand;</li>
<li>exclusivity within a geographic area;</li>
<li>a particular profit margin;</li>
<li>continued availability of credit;</li>
<li>continuation of a particular product indefinitely; or</li>
<li>any particular commercial outcome from stocking Apex Feeds products.</li>
</ul>
<p>Nothing in this clause affects obligations concerning orders already accepted or rights that cannot lawfully be excluded.</p>
<h4 id="s36-13">36.13 No Geographic Exclusivity</h4>
<p>Unless Apex Feeds expressly agrees otherwise in writing, Authorised Retailer status is non-exclusive. Apex Feeds may appoint other Authorised Retailers, supply other customers or sell through its own authorised channels.</p>
<h4 id="s36-14">36.14 Continuing Obligation to Update Information</h4>
<p>The Retailer agrees to notify Apex Feeds of material changes to information relevant to its Authorised Retailer status as required by this Agreement, including applicable changes to ownership, legal entity, ABN, authorised locations or primary wholesale contact information.</p>
<h4 id="s36-15">36.15 Electronic Acceptance</h4>
<p>Where this Agreement is accepted electronically, the Retailer’s authorised electronic acceptance has the same intended contractual effect as signing a physical copy, to the extent permitted by applicable law. Apex Feeds may retain an electronic record of the acceptance and the version of the Agreement accepted.</p>
<h4 id="s36-16">36.16 Voluntary Acceptance</h4>
<p>The Retailer confirms that it is entering the wholesale relationship voluntarily and may choose not to participate in the Apex Feeds wholesale program if it does not wish to accept the applicable terms. Once accepted, the Agreement applies until terminated, replaced or otherwise dealt with in accordance with its terms.</p>
<h4 id="s36-17">36.17 Non-Excludable Rights</h4>
<p>Nothing in this acknowledgement constitutes a waiver of any right, guarantee, remedy or protection that cannot lawfully be waived, excluded, restricted or modified.</p>

